      "skill_id": "fr-a1-025",
      "title": "Necessity and prohibition: il faut + infinitive",
      "explanation": "Il faut followed by an infinitive says what has to be done in general: Il faut travailler (one has to work, you have to work). Il faut never changes for person or number. In the negative, il ne faut pas followed by an infinitive says what must not be done: Il ne faut pas parler ici (you must not speak here). It is a prohibition, not just a lack of need.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "fr": "Il faut travailler.",
          "en": "One has to work."
        },
        {
          "fr": "Il faut jouer dehors.",
          "en": "You have to play outside."
        },
        {
          "fr": "Il ne faut pas parler ici.",
          "en": "You must not speak here."
        }
      ],
      "references": ["FEI-INV"],
