    {
      "skill_id": "fr-a1-027",
      "title": "Professions and nationalities: masculine and feminine",
      "explanation": "After être, a profession or nationality usually has no article: Il est médecin, Elle est française. Many words add -e for the feminine: étudiant, étudiante; français, française; allemand, allemande; américain, américaine. Words in -ien double the n: italien, italienne. Words in -ier become -ière: infirmier, infirmière; boulanger, boulangère. Some end in -eur and change: acteur, actrice. Words already ending in -e do not change: journaliste, dentiste. Nationality adjectives are written with a lowercase letter.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "fr": "Elle est étudiante.",
          "en": "She is a student."
        },
        {
          "fr": "Il est français.",
          "en": "He is French."
        },
        {
          "fr": "Marie est italienne.",
          "en": "Marie is Italian."
        }
      ],
      "references": ["FEI-INV", "DELF-A1-ADULT"],
      "version": {
