      "skill_id": "fr-a1-028",
      "title": "Action in progress: être en train de + infinitive",
      "explanation": "To stress that an action is happening right now, use the present of être, then en train de, then an infinitive: Je suis en train de chanter. De becomes d' before a vowel or a silent h: Elle est en train d'écouter. The infinitive does not change. The simple present can also express an action in progress, but être en train de makes it clear that it is happening at this moment.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "fr": "Je suis en train de chanter.",
          "en": "I am singing right now."
        },
        {
          "fr": "Il est en train de regarder la télé.",
          "en": "He is watching TV right now."
        },
        {
          "fr": "Ils sont en train d'arriver.",
          "en": "They are arriving right now."
        }
      ],
      "references": ["FEI-INV"],
